    lines+=['','R1 has104,012 trainable parameters; R2 has157,516. C1 has156,716; C2 and C3 each157,516. C2 sees complete3600-sample numerical response curves, while C3 uses12 fixed generic smooth spectral functions. R2 additionally receives external FSPS spectra and IGM response information. These controls do not make the physical information identical. R0 canonical slots has113,900 parameters. R1_brightness is a separate fixed source-only ablation, never chosen using targets.','','![Transfer comparison](cross_survey_summary.png)','','![Target PDFs and calibration](target_predictions_calibration.png)','','## Source learning and optimization limits','','![Source learning](source_learning.png)','','| Source/model | Best step | Source CE | Source outliers | Final plateau |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
    for r in models:lines.append(f"|{r['source']}/{r['arm']} seed{r['seed']}|{r['best_update']}|{r['validation_metrics']['ce']:.3f}|{r['validation_metrics']['outlier_fraction']:.4f}|{r['final_plateau']}|")
    nplateau=sum(r['final_plateau'] for r in models if r['arm'] in ['R1','R2']);lines+=['',f'{nplateau}/12 primary runs meet the registered final plateau condition. Meaningful source learning is established, but improvement from initialization is not proof of convergence. Common2500/5000 snapshots are reported in common_update_metrics.csv. Any remaining improvement or architecture-dependent underfitting limits a fully optimized architecture ranking. The primary checkpoint remains minimum source-validation CE, as locked before T2 access.','','## Selection, support, and high redshift','',f"T2 median positive i AB magnitude is{support['T2']['i_magnitude'][2]:.2f}, versus{support['unlabeled_population']['i_magnitude'][2]:.2f} in the4096-object unlabeled local photometric sample. Source-defined common photometric support is{support['T2']['common_support_fraction']:.2%} for T2 and{support['unlabeled_population']['common_support_fraction']:.2%} for the unlabeled population. Successful bright/spectroscopic-subset inference would not establish full faint-population accuracy.",'','The entire recovered historical Legacy training population has zero z≥2 objects, measured directly. HSC likewise lacks z≥2 supervision. The eligible deduplicated Mixed source has80,399 training galaxies and20,297 validation galaxies; one deterministic observed view per shared galaxy prevents repeated-view weighting, followed by balanced source-survey batches. The high-z target stratum is unsupported extrapolation, never supervised high-z confirmation. Conditional redshift, source brightness/SNR and usable-band results are preserved; no subgroup is selected to rescue the primary endpoint.','','## Physical baselines and observational controls','','D12 is a measured-error, free-amplitude NNLS profile pseudo-posterior with uniform redshift density. D2 is a constrained diagnostic using the previous fixed two-template basis; its real-galaxy mismatch remains a limitation. Neither is added to R2 logits. Their full/HSC/overlap results and calibration remain in target_metrics.csv, including large CE or overconfidence. Wrong-response metadata keeps measured flux fixed and is an inconsistency stress test. Fresh fixed128-SED D2 simulations regenerate coherent HSC/Legacy/full photometry with independent SNR40 noise; they are an explicitly matched-family synthetic positive control, not real target evidence. Actual S3 views keep source-validation galaxies paired and do not become an independent population.','','## Frozen Qwen and historical exploratory sample','','The original frozen HSC QLoRA/PDF checkpoint passed a32-object replay with exactly zero logit/PDF discrepancy. Label-free predictions were made for all frozen T2 identities using actual grizy fluxes with native source fields/order/precision and explicit unavailable MW_EBV. No Qwen training or tuning occurred. Its five-band and missing-EBV interface differs from full11-band numerical information; compare the same T2 objects and HSC-restricted numerical predictions. HSC PDR2 aliases and response/exposure assumptions, terminal-token fragility and missing metadata remain explicit limitations.']
    q=[r for r in rows if 'Qwen' in r['condition']]
