    lines+=['','T1 remains the historical256-object ZPHOT agreement diagnostic. Its separately labelled predictions and tables are exploratory and cannot confirm true-redshift transfer or faint-population accuracy. T3 was not added.','','## Reproducibility and decision','','Dataset and protocol hashes are under Stage3A. Model checkpoints, learning curves, common snapshots, source-only selection, finite PDFs, target eligibility, per-galaxy predictions, PIT histograms, paired bootstrap intervals and exact source/target exclusions are saved here. Benchmark hash and source model lock precede target_labels_opened.json. Original Stage0–2 results remain protected. Training runtime/memory and CPU inference budgets are recorded separately; peak GPU allocation is the cumulative process peak up to each arm, not an isolated model allocation. No large sweep, pretrained-Qwen training, or Stage2C was launched.','','Read the joint assessment for the ten requested scientific decisions. The next foundation-model comparison requires matched observations, paired independent spectroscopy, stronger high-z/faint-source coverage, source convergence, a frozen-backbone comparator and a controlled pretraining/randomization design. Stage2C is deferred pending those requirements.']
